  "term": "spontaneous neural activity",
  "definition": "Spontaneous neural activity is the brain’s ongoing activity, considered here as a biological process that can be studied in people with subclinical depression. Examining it may help reveal brain-related features of this mild depressive state and possible risk for later major depressive disorder.",
